KG42.register("rules-c34a30f0f74b28f677bd149b",{"id":"28-multiclass_prosumer_preferences::v141-c-R008","paper":"28-multiclass_prosumer_preferences","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R008","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Prosumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"Small-scale prosumers are allowed to trade energy with one another and with the wholesale market within the proposed P2P platform. Scope: Small-scale prosumer participation in the proposed distribution-network P2P platform. Individual prosumers are programmed to operate as competitive price-takers. Scope: Assumed operating model of individual prosumers within the proposed P2P platform. Prosumers could be represented within the P2P platform by their retail supplier acting on their behalf based on their energy preferences. Scope: Optional retail-supplier representation of prosumers within the proposed P2P platform. Condition: If prosumers contract with retail suppliers to obtain predictable energy prices.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.prosumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.prosumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Assumed operating model of individual prosumers within the proposed P2P platform. | Optional retail-supplier representation of prosumers within the proposed P2P platform. | Small-scale prosumer participation in the proposed distribution-network P2P platform.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E36","v141-b-g01-E10"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Small-scale prosumers are allowed to trade energy with one another and with the wholesale market within the proposed P2P platform. Scope: Small-scale prosumer participation in the proposed distribution-network P2P platform.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E36"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Individual prosumers are programmed to operate as competitive price-takers. Scope: Assumed operating model of individual prosumers within the proposed P2P platform.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Prosumers could be represented within the P2P platform by their retail supplier acting on their behalf based on their energy preferences. Scope: Optional retail-supplier representation of prosumers within the proposed P2P platform. Condition: If prosumers contract with retail suppliers to obtain predictable energy prices.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E36"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"exception","statement":"If the stated competition conditions are not met over the long term, the platform owner/prosumers with market power may need to be compensated to incentivise their participation. Scope: Long-term condition on the assumed competitive price-taking operation of the proposed P2P platform.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-G01-E36","location":{"location_id":"src-96285c344a-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. Principle of Operation","anchor_text":"PEER-TO-PEER ENERGY TRADING DRIVEN 4007 wholesale market without a retail supplier. However, retail ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"The proposed P2P energy market platform allows small-scale prosumers to trade energy with one another, and with the wholesale market, rather than relying on a traditional retail supplier. However, retail suppliers could still have an important role, providing services such as invoicing, real-time metering and local energy management [35]. Also, small-scale prosumers may not wish to be exposed to fluctuating wholesale energy prices. Prosumers could contract with retail suppliers to obtain predictable energy prices, and then their supplier could act on their behalf within the P2P platform based on their energy preferences."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-96285c344a-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. Principle of Operation","anchor_text":"the current trading interval, the trading interval recedes by a t0 step and the prosumers update the","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"It is assumed that the P2P energy market platform operates as a price-taker in the wholesale electricity market. The platform agent is programmed to set prices that maximise social welfare, and the individual prosumers are programmed to operate as competitive price-takers. This is desirable for all participants if the platform owner faces competition from other potential platforms, so it cannot set prices to maximise profits, and there are sufficient prosumers so that they cannot improve their position through strategic price-setting behaviour [33]. If these conditions are not met over the long term, the platform owner/prosumers with market power may need to be compensated to incentivise their participation."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No decision or design variable is defined by the source for this participation rule. The source statements permit or describe prosumer trading, price-taking behavior, and optional retail-supplier representation; 'participation.prosumer' is a role/process node, not a quantitative variable.","empty_theta_reason":"No numeric threshold, coefficient, or parameter is specified for this participation rule. The rule's source statements concern permissions, behavioral assumptions, and a conditional market-power compensation exception, not parameterized optimization constraints."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.prosumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-G01-E36","quote":"The proposed P2P energy market platform allows small-scale prosumers to trade energy with one another, and with the wholesale market, rather than relying on a traditional retail supplier."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E10","quote":"the individual prosumers are programmed to operate as competitive price-takers."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-G01-E36","quote":"Prosumers could contract with retail suppliers to obtain predictable energy prices, and then their supplier could act on their behalf within the P2P platform based on their energy preferences."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"c8242a38f75293a3b0a4b995ab4064ea488fa57055b4cade85abf8eece08728a","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The supplied evidence for this rule states participation permissions, assumed price-taking behavior, optional retail-supplier representation, and a long-term market-power compensation exception. These are procedural/admission and behavioral conditions; the quoted source text for this rule provides no equation, objective, formal constraint, variable domain, or numeric parameter to formalize. B evidence remains unreviewed.","bindings":[],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
